2 CONT Princess of Egypt
1 NOTE OR "NITETIS"; b. ca. 570 BC
1 NOTE Cyrus fell ill and sent to Amasis of Egypt for a physician. Amasis pickedon who having wife and family was very reluctant to go, but he was ordered, and had to go. he cured Cyrus. And fomr skill he gained great influence in court.
2 CONC  To "get even" he mentioned that Amasis had a very beautiful daughter, and Cyrus sent to Amasis to have that daughter as wife. Amasis could not very well refuse, but also could not bear to think of parting with his daughter. So he
2 CONC  instead sent Nitetis.  Nitetis had been held more or elss prisoner, and was both talented and beautiful, and Cyrus was pleased. His other wife Cassandane, and her children Cambyses and Smerdis hated her. Cambyses vowed to goto Eg
2 CONC ypt and turn the country upside down as soon as he was king and did just that.
