1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Perhaps the same  as https://www.geni.com/people/N-N/6000000056402509942, husband of https://www.geni.com/people/Pancalo/6000000015565536487?through=6000000056402509942
2 CONT *Father of https://www.geni.com/people/Bardas-I/6000000026443435344 in DIY online trees  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna, who married Hmayeak, a Mamikonian prince (died c. 797), by whom she had '''Konstantinos''', an officer at the court of [https://www.geni.com/people/Michael-III-Byzantine-Emperor/6000000003051267350 Emperor Michael III].[17][
2 CONC 18]
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leo_V_the_Armenian
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Relationships are not proven.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00215847&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is known of Konstantinos other than that he was the son of Hmayeak/Maiactes/Myakes, a noble from Adrianople/Hadrianopolis (modern-day Edirne in Thrace, the westernmost part of Turkey) and an unnamed daughter of Leo V 'the A
2 CONC rmenian', emperor of Byzantium, and that he was held captive by the Bulgars from 813 until 828. His marriage to https://www.geni.com/people/Pankalo/6000000015565536487?through=6000000056402509942  [??] would produce another empero
2 CONC r of Byzantium, [https://www.geni.com/people/Basil-I-Byzantine-Emperor/6000000002434099128?through=6000000015565536487 Basilius I 'the Macedonian'], as well as a son https://www.geni.com/people/Bardas-I/6000000026443435344?through
2 CONC =6000000003645912098, ?? both of whom would have progeny. Konstantinos is believed to have died between 838 and as early as 827 or as late as about 840.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * http://erwan.gil.free.fr/modules/freepages/pharaons/ramses_II.pdf page 13 - 14
2 CONT * https://www.genealogieonline.nl/balogh-family-tree/I31011.php
2 CONT * https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00215847&tree=LEO cites 
2 CONT *~Genealogists' Magazine, Journal of the Society of Genealogists, London. Mar 1991 
2 CONT *Nos Ancêtres de l'Antiquité Paris, 1991 , Settipani, Christian. 187 
2 CONT
