1 NOTE RBS : Adarnase I, Prince of Eushet'i-Artani was appointed by the Greeks as erist'avi of the regions of Armenia. Co-heir of Cholarzene-Javakhet'i. Prince of Eushet'i-Artani. He acquired, while Juansher was still alive, a third of K
2 CONC larjhet'i, Shavshet'i, Achara, Nigali, Asisp'ori, Artan, and Lower Tao, and those fortresses which the descendants of King Vaxt'ang possessed. Also called Atrnerseh. He was according to one well-known legend to descend from the ho
2 CONC use of the prophet David. He was given Rhisha, Shghuer, and Atone by King Arch'il circa 736. He died before 813 at Klarjheti, Transcaucasia.
