1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''NOTE:''' Alp Arslan has a cousin of hers (a daughter of her paternal uncle Smbat of Lori) listed as a wife. It's possible that sources confuse the two woman and are unclear which king of Lori gave his daughter t
2 CONC o Alp Arslan as a wife. For now, both will be listed as his wife until decisive evidence is found.
2 CONT
2 CONT * From page 75 of ''The History of Armenia'' by Simon Payaslian, 2007:
2 CONT
2 CONT When Kyuriké I (r. 1048-1089) succeeded his father, the Seljuk invasions into Armenia had intensified. In 1064, Alp Aslan led his army into the land of Lori and, after much bloodshed and pillage, demanded Kyuiké's daughter for wif
2 CONC e. The king of Lori refused at first, but further negotiations and mediation by the Abkhazian king Bagrat IV convinced him that the failure to grant his daughter's hand to Sultan Alp Aslan would aggravate the already grave situati
2 CONC on. By then the Bagratuni kingdoms at Ani and Kars had collapsed, leaving the kingdom of Lori as the only Armenian stronghold.
