1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Farrukhzad I was the 24th ruler of Shirvanshahs. He was fourth son of Shirvanshah Manuchehr III, younger brother of previous shahs - Shirvanshah Afridun II, Akhsitan I, Shirvanshah Shahanshah, uncle of Shirvanshah 
2 CONC Fariburz II and father of Shirvanshah Gushtasb I and Prince Rashid ibn Farrukhzad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign Nor his reign period, neither any coin minted during his reign is known. His name is known via epigraphic evidence.[1] Epitaph on Round tower of Mardakan refers to Shirvanshah Gushtasb I as "Gershasb b. Farrukhzad b. Manuche
2 CONC hr" with date of Hijri, Dhu al-Hijjah 600 (August, 1204). Epitaph on Pir Hussayn Khanqah mentions his name also as grandfather of Shirvanshah Fariburz III. Also, an epitaph on Pir Mardakan Khanqah mentions his name as "Greatest pa
2 CONC dishah, khagan, Farrukhzad b. Fazilalmuwahhid Manuchehr".[2] He probably died in same year because of old age.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Farrukhzad_I
