2 CONC e passage which of Emperor Mikhael VIII's brothers is indicated.  If it refers to Ioannes, this was the daughter of his wife --- Tornikaine, assuming that the text is accurate.  She is shown in Europäische Stammtafeln[905] as the 
2 CONC daughter of Ioannes Palaiologos by his second marriage.  If the latter is correct, she must have been a child bride.  The Georgian Chronicle (18th century) records that the wife of King Davit was "la reine, fille du grand Paléolog
