1 NOTE {geni:about_me} After Anna Angelina died in 1212, Theodore married secondly Philippa of Armenia (1183-aft. 1219), a daughter of King Ruben III of Armenia. This marriage was annulled a year later for religious reasons and they divo
2 CONC rced in 1216, and the son born to them, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Konstantinos Laskaris, born in 1214, was disinherited, being created Duke of Thrace afterwards.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theodore_I_Laskaris
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of King Ruben III of Armenia
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ARMENIA.htm#PhilippaM1ShahninshahM2TheodorosINikaia
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         PHILIPPA (1183-before 1219).  The Chronique du Royaume de la Petite Arménie of Constable Sempad records that Lewon arranged the marriage of "Schahenscah [l'autre fils de Tchordouanel]" and "la fille cadette de Roupen, P
2 CONC hilippa qui vivait auprès de [Ritha] mère de Léon" in [3 Feb 1189/4 Feb 1190][522].  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Aalis et Phelippe" as the two daughters of "Rupin de la Montaigne qui estoit seignor d'Ermenie" & his wife, specify
2 CONC ing that Philippa was wife of "Lascre" and had a son "Costans qui fu mort"[523].  The Chronique du Royaume de la Petite Arménie of Constable Sempad records the betrothal of "Philippa fille de mon frère" and Oshin, oldest son of "H
2 CONC éthoum, fils d'Oschin", at the end of the section dealing with the year [31 Jan 1198/30 Jan 1199][524].  Smbat Sparapet's Chronicle records that "King Lewon…previously had…made marriage relations with Emperor Lascari and gave to h
2 CONC im as a wife Philippa, the daughter of his brother Ruben" in [27 Jan 1216/25 Jan 1217][525].  Georgius Akropolites records that "Theodorum Lascarim imperatorem" married "ex Armeniis uxorem" after his first wife died, but sent her 
2 CONC back "in Ciliciam illius patriam"[526].  Her second marriage was arranged by her future husband with her uncle, Lewon I King of Armenia, presumably to obtain Armenian support for the newly emerged empire at Nikaia.  Gardner refers
2 CONC  to the theory that Philippa was repudiated by her second husband because he had expected to marry King Lewon's daughter (who was married to Jean de Brienne King of Jerusalem about the same time) and that he sent Philippa home aft
2 CONC er discovering that he had been duped into marrying Lewon's niece instead[527].  
