2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raden_Wijaya
2 CONT
2 CONT (1293-1309)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to later controversial source from 17th century, Pustaka Rajyarajya i Bhumi Nusantara, Raden Wijaya was the son of Rakeyan Jayadarma (son of Sunda-Galuh King Prabu Guru Darmasiksa) and Dyah Lembu Tal (daughter of Mahisa 
2 CONC Campaka from Singhasari). Rakeyan Jayadarma was poisoned and after her husband's death, Dyah Lembu Tal returned from Sunda-Galuh Kingdom to Singhasari with Raden Wijaya. This story is similar to that of Babad Tanah Jawi which ment
2 CONC ioned the founder of Majapahit was Jaka Sesuruh, a son from the king of Pajajaran's which is located in Sunda Kingdom. Jaka Sesuruh ran to the east because of a rivalry with his step brother Siyung Wanara.[4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://greatsunda.wordpress.com/category/history-of-sunda/
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rakeyan Jayadharma, son of Dharmasiksa, married Dyah Lembu Tal of Singhasari, and have a son Wijaya. Jayadharma died in boyhood and Dyah lembu Tal returned to Singhasari. Wijaya later established Majapahit. Rakeyan Saunggalah, Jay
2 CONC adharma’s brother, succeeded Dharmasiksa.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Membuka negeri baru Majapahit dengan bantuan orang Madura, di atas tanah di desa Tarik yang dianugerahi Jayakatwang setelah jatuhnya Singhasari. bergabung dengan tentera Tiongkok (Kubali Khan) yang menyerang Singhasari untuk menen
2 CONC tang Jayakatwang dan kemudian menyerang pula tentera Tiongkok apabila mereka kembali ke pelabuhan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raja Majapahit 1293-1309M begelar Krtarajasa Jayawardhana.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT I was the first King of the Majapahit Empire and I ruled from 1293 to 1309.
2 CONT
2 CONT I am popularly known as Nararya Sangramawijaya (stylized as: Kertarajasa Jayawardhana). I am also known as Dyah Wijaya in my early days.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Raja Majapahit pertama adalah Reden Wijaya yang bergelar Kertarajasa Jayawardhana. Pararaton memberitakan bahwa Raden Wijaya naik tahta tahun çaka 1216 (= 1294 M). Demikian juga dengan Negarakretagama memberikan penanggalan tahun 
2 CONC yang sama
2 CONT
2 CONT Pararaton :
2 CONT
2 CONT “ ..… samangka raden wijaya ajejeng prabhhu i çaka rasa rupa dwi citanggu, 1216…. “
2 CONT
2 CONT Negarakretagama (45:1) :
2 CONT
2 CONT “ … ri pjah nrpa jayakatwan awa tikang jagat alilan masa rupa rawi  cakabda rika nararyya sira ratu siniwin pura ri majapahit tanuraga jayaripu tinlah nrpa krtarajasa jayawardhana nrpati …..”
2 CONT
2 CONT Kidung Harsawijaya, Raden Wijaya naik tahta tepat pada purneng kartika masa panca dasi çaka 1215 (= 1293 M) yaitu pada tanggal 15 saat rembulan purnama bulan Kartika tahun çaka 1216 (= 1294 M) yang bertepatan dengan tanggal 10 Nov
2 CONC ember 1293. Sementara menurut prasasti Kudadu pada bulan Bhadrawapada çaka 1216 (= 1294 M) Raden Wijaya telah disebut Kartarajasajaya Jayawardhana nama rajabhiseka.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kidung Harsyawijaya (Demung VI Kidung 84-b dab 85-b) menuliskan :
2 CONT
2 CONT   “ Lah iya ujarira anging mben ikapanjang punang diwasayu ri purneng kerttikamasa iku abecik. Tan-dwa prapta pancadaci cukleng kacatur ndan siradhipati enjang mangkyangdani pan bhyuhan ing karya punang wong atrewuh aliweran jalw 
2 CONC istriprasama aky’amundut swidhiwidhana krama ning homa bhiseka prabu ri purwa ning pangstryan tang pangasthulan”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yang artinya kurang lebih :
2 CONT
2 CONT   “ Hanya demikianlah katanya, bahwa besuk hari lusa harikelima belas bulan Kartika adalah bulan baik. Tak lama kemudian telah sampailah pada waktunya, tanggal lima belas waktu purnama ke empat, pada pagi hari sang adhipati telah 
2 CONC hanyut dalam tugas pekerjaannya, semua orang juga kelihatan sibuk laki-laki perempuan mempersiapkan untaian kalung dan boreh konyoh untuk dipersembahkan pada awal pelantikan”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Selanjutnya Raden Wijaya sebagi pendiri kerajaan Majapahit memerintah selama 16 tahun (çaka 1215 – 1231 (= 1293 – 1309 M). Menurut Pararaton, Raden Wijaya meninggal pada tahun çaka 1267 (= 1345 M) dan didharmakan di Antahpura “ ….
2 CONC . mokta sira, dhinarma ring antahpura i çaka 1257 … “ (Par). Namun kitab Negerakretagama memberitakan bahwa Raden Wijaya meninggal pada tahun çaka 1231 (= 1209 M) didharmakan di Simping dengan Ciwaistis dan di Antahpura dengan sif
2 CONC at Budhis (Nag. 47:3)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Berkuasa tahun 1294M (1216S). Beliau memperistri keempat putri Kertanagara / Siwa Budha Tumapel. Melarikan diri dari serbuan Kublai Khan yang memporak porandakan Singasari dan menetap di Majapahit (sekarang Trowulan). Dibantu oleh
2 CONC  Penguasa Madura Arya Wiraraja memulai pemerintahan baru. Januari 1293 beliau bergabung dengan Mongol menghabisi Jayakatwang, yang menguasai sisa-sisa kerajaan mertuanya Singasari. Bulan Maret 1293 kekuatan gabungan Mongol dan Maj
2 CONC apahit menggilas kerajaan Kediri. Pada saat Mongol lengah, beliau menyerang secara mendadak. Mongol mengalami kekalahan dan meninggalkan Pulau Jawa. November tahun itu juga, beliau menjadi raja Mojopahit bergelar Kertarajasa Jayaw
2 CONC ardana. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jayanegara / Raden Kolo Gemet
2 CONT
2 CONT Tri Buwana Tungga Dewi / Bhre Kahuripan II 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT First king of Majapahit
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sumber : http://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raden_Wijaya
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Silsilah Keluarga'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Raden Wijaya dalam prasasti Balawi tahun 1305 menyatakan dirinya sebagai anggota Wangsa Rajasa. Menurut Nagarakretagama, Wijaya adalah putra Dyah Lembu Tal, putra Narasinghamurti. Menurut Pararaton, Narasinghamurti alias Mahisa Ca
2 CONC mpaka adalah putra Mahisa Wonga Teleng putra Ken Arok pendiri Wangsa Rajasa. [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Menurut prasasti Balawi dan Nagarakretagama, Raden Wijaya menikah dengan empat orang putri Kertanagara, raja terakhir Kerajaan Singhasari, yaitu Tribhuwaneswari, Narendraduhita, Jayendradewi, dan Gayatri. Sedangkan menurut Pararat
2 CONC on, ia hanya menikahi dua orang putri Kertanagara saja, serta seorang putri dari Kerajaan Malayu bernama Dara Petak, yaitu salah satu dari dua putri yang dibawa kembali dari Melayu oleh pasukan yang dulunya dikirim oleh Kertanagar
2 CONC a yang dikenal dengan nama Ekspedisi Pamalayu pada masa kerajaan Singhasari. Dara Petak merupakan salah seorang putri Srimat Tribhuwanaraja Mauliwarmadewa Raja Melayu dari Kerajaan Dharmasraya [2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Menurut prasasti Sukamerta dan prasasti Balawi, Raden Wijaya memiliki seorang putra dari Tribhuwaneswari bernama Jayanagara.[3]Sedangkan Jayanagara menurut Pararaton adalah putra Dara Petak, dan menurut Nagarakretagama adalah putr
2 CONC a Indreswari. Sementara itu, dari Gayatri lahir dua orang putri bernama Dyah Gitarja dan Dyah Wiyat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Namun demikian ada juga pendapat lain, dimana Raden Wijaya juga mengambil Dara Jingga yang juga salah seorang putri Kerajaan Melayu sebagai istrinya selain dari Dara Petak, karena Dara Jingga juga dikenal memiliki sebutan sira ala
2 CONC ki dewa — dia yang dinikahi orang yang bergelar dewa.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raden_Wijaya
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Raden Wijaya or Raden Vijaya (also known as Nararya Sangramawijaya, regnal name Kertarajasa Jayawardhana) (reigned 1293–1309) was a Javanese emperor, and the founder and first monarch of the Majapahit Empire.[1] The history of his
2 CONC  founding of Majapahit was written in several records, including Pararaton and Negarakertagama.[2] His rule was marked by the victory against the army and the Mongol navy of Kublai Khan's Yuan dynasty.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry
2 CONT There are several versions of his ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Pararaton, Raden Wijaya was the son of Mahisa Campaka, prince of Singhasari.Mahisa Campaka alias Narasingamurti is the son of Mahisa Wonga Teleng. Meanwhile, Mahisa Wonga Teleng was the son of Ken Arok, founder of the
2 CONC  Rajasa dynasty.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT According to later controversial source from 17th century, Pustaka Rajyarajya i Bhumi Nusantara, Raden Wijaya was the son of Rakeyan Jayadarma (son of Sunda-Galuh King Prabu Guru Darmasiksa) and Dyah Lembu Tal (daughter of Mahisa 
2 CONC Campaka from Singhasari). Rakeyan Jayadarma was poisoned and after her husband's death, Dyah Lembu Tal returned from Sunda-Galuh Kingdom to Singhasari with Raden Wijaya. This story is similar to that of Babad Tanah Jawi which ment
2 CONC ioned the founder of Majapahit was Jaka Sesuruh, a son from the king of Pajajaran's which is located in Sunda Kingdom. Jaka Sesuruh ran to the east because of a rivalry with his step brother Siyung Wanara.[4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternatively with Nagarakretagama, Dyah Lembu Tal, also known as Dyah Singhamurti, was a man and the great-grandson of Ken Arok, king of Singhasari (1222–1227) and Ken Dedes, by their son Mahisa Wonga Teleng, and his son Mahisa C
2 CONC ampaka (Nara Singhamurti). Because Nagarakretagama was written in 1365, 56 years since the Raden Wijaya's death, popular opinion supports it.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Prior to the founding of Majapahit
2 CONT In 1289, Kublai Khan sent a demand for tribute to the Kingdom of Singhasari, although the demand was refused by Kertanagara, King of Singhasari and the messenger was humiliated with his ear cut off.[6] Shortly after, there was a r
2 CONC ebellion against Singhasari in the duchy of Gelang-Gelang (modern day Madiun) led by Jayakatwang. Kertanagara was killed in the attempt to put down the rebellion in 1292, and Raden Wijaya fled to Sumenep, Madura, along with the go
2 CONC vernor of that region, Arya Wiraraja. There, Raden Wijaya made a plan to establish a new kingdom. Wijaya promised that he would divide Java with Arya Wiraraja if Arya Wiraraja could help him overthrow Jayakatwang's Kediri kingdom 
2 CONC . When he was young, Wiraraja served Narasingamurti, Raden Wijaya's grandfather. So, he was willing to help the prince to overthrow Jayakatwang. Raden Wijaya vowed that if he succeeded in reclaiming his father in law's throne, his
2 CONC  power would be divided into two, namely for himself and for Wiraraja. In 1293 the Mongol army came to punish Kertanagara who dared to harm Kublai Khan's envoy in 1289. Raden Wijaya as Kertanagara's heir was ready to hand over him
2 CONC self as long as he is first helped to liberate himself from Jayakatwang. So the Mongol and Majapahit troops joined forces to invade the capital city of Kadiri. At that time, the Kingdom of Kediri collapsed. Next, Raden Wijaya base
2 CONC d on Wiraraja's input attacked the Mongol army who were experiencing the euphoria of victory against the Kediri Kingdom. Inevitably, Wiraraja with his various tactics brought victory to Raden Wijaya to defeat the Mongol army. This
2 CONC  was the starting point for Raden Wijaya to come to power and make Tarik (Trowulan, Mojokerto) the center of power which later became the Majapahit Kingdom. The term Majapahit emerged because in the Tarik forest area there are man
2 CONC y maja (mojo) fruits which taste bitter. Raden Wijaya became the first king of Majapahit which became independent in 1293. Arya Wiraraja was appointed as the pasangguhan/ senapati (warlord) of Majapahit with the title Rakryan Mant
2 CONC ri Arya Wiraraja Makapramuka.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Arya Wiraraja's son Ranggalawe served as one of Wijaya's adipati/ duke but in later days he would rebel against the new king. Other famous officers were Lembu Sora and Nambi, both also rebelled against Wijaya respectively after th
2 CONC e founding of Majapahit kingdom.The trigger for rebellion is that even though those who rebel have been given positions, they still feel dissatisfied.[8][9] Ranggalawe rebellion was the first recorded in 1295. Ranggalawe lost in h
2 CONC is battle against the Majapahit Kingdom and died at the hands of Mahisa Anabrang while fighting at the Tambak Beras river. Lembu Sora rebellion occurred in 1301. War between the Majapahit army and Lembu Sora's followers could not 
2 CONC be avoided. Lembu Sora and his followers Juru Demung and Gajah Biru died in this battle. Nambi rebellion occurred during the reign of King Jayanegara, it is stated that during the reign of Jayanegara, Nambi rebellion occurred. The
2 CONC n Nambi rebellion was suppressed in 1316.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Foundation of the Majapahit kingdom
2 CONT In November 1292, a Mongol force landed in Tuban, East Java, with the aim of revenge for Kertanagara's humiliation of the Mongol messenger. However, Kertanegara was already dead. Raden Wijaya initially made an alliance with the Mo
2 CONC ngols with the aim of attacking Kediri, which had become the strongest country in Java. Jayakatwang was defeated and destroyed in 1293, at which point Raden Wijaya turned and attacked the Mongol force. The Mongols, already weakene
2 CONC d by tropical diseases, the climate, and imperial overreach, were forced to flee Java.[11] Raden Vijaya then established the Majapahit kingdom, taking the title Kritarajasa Jayavardhana.[12]: 201, 232–233 
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal life
2 CONT According to George Coedes, prior to the fall of Singhasari, Wijaya was married to Gayatri Rajapatni, the daughter of Kertanegara, King of Singhasari. However, during the formation of the new kingdom Majapahit, he married the four
2 CONC  daughters of Kertanegara.
2 CONT
2 CONT The siblings were Parameswari Tribhuwana the oldest, Prajnaparamitha, Narendra Duhita, and Gayatri Rajapatni the youngest. The reasons of Raden Wijaya's practice of siblings polygamy was to ensure his claim of legitimacy, also to 
2 CONC prevent the contest for Kertanegara's Singhasari legacy. Raden Wijaya also took Indreswari (also known as Dara Petak), supposedly a princess of Malayu Dharmasraya Kingdom brought by Kebo Anabrang to Majapahit court from Sumatra th
2 CONC rough Kertanegara's Pamalayu expedition. Pararaton mentioned that Kala Gemet was born by Dara Petak, the Dharmasraya princess, while Nagarakretagama mentioned that he was born by Indreswari, leading to assumption that Indreswari w
2 CONC as another name of Dara Petak. King Kertarajasa Jayawardhana has five wives, however in his posthumous portrayal as the god Harihara in Simping temple, his image was flanked by two female figures, suggested that he has two pramesv
2 CONC ari (queen consort), one is Gayatri, the other is Tribhuwana or probably Dara Petak.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses and Children
2 CONT Supreme Queen
2 CONT
2 CONT Rajapatni Sri Rajendra Dyah Dewī Gayatri
2 CONT the youngest daughter of King Kertanegara of Singhasari
2 CONT Queen
2 CONT
2 CONT Sri Parameswari Dyah Dewī Tribhuwaneswari
2 CONT the eldest daughter of King Kertanegara of Singhasari
2 CONT Consorts
2 CONT
2 CONT Sri Mahadewī Dyah Dewī Narendraduhita
2 CONT daughter of King Kertanegara of Singhasari
2 CONT Sri Jayendra Dyah Dewī Prajña Paramita
2 CONT daughter of King Kertanegara of Singhasari
2 CONT Sri Indreswari
2 CONT born as Dara Petak, daughter of King Srimat Tribhuwanaraja Mauliawarmadewa of Dharmasraya
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Tribhuwana, 3rd Queen of Majapahit
2 CONT born as Dyah Tya, daughter of Gayatri
2 CONT Jayanagara, 2nd King of Majapahit
2 CONT son of Dara Petak
2 CONT Rajadewi Maharajasa, 2nd Princess of Daha
2 CONT born as Dyah Wiyat, daughter of Gayatri
2 CONT Rule of Majapahit
2 CONT Raden Wijaya was known as a firm and capable ruler. Aria Wiraraja who had been so useful during the period of the establishment of the kingdom, was given Madura, which was granted a special status. He was also given an autonomous 
2 CONC region around Lumajang and the Blambangan Peninsula, and his son, Nambi, was appointed Prime Minister. Raden Wijaya also formed a special army guard for the king which consists of 7 people named Ra Kuti, Ra Semi, Ra Tanca, Ra Wede
2 CONC ng, Ra Yuyu, Ra Banyak, and Ra Pangsa
2 CONT
2 CONT Heir
2 CONT From his wife Indreswari, Raden Wijaya had a son, Dyah Jayanegara. From his wife Gayatri Rajapatni, he had two daughters, Tribhuwana Wijayatunggadewi and Rajadewi. Other wives seemed to be childless, including his first wife, Trib
2 CONC huwana.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, Raden Wijaya was succeeded by his son, Jayanegara.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT According to the Nagarakretagama, King Wijaya died in 1309. He was buried in the Simping Temple (id) as "Harihara",[13] the combination of Vishnu and Shiva.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his son Jayanegara.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also
2 CONT Senapati of Mataram, the founder and first king of Mataram Sultanate was a descendant of Raden Wijaya
