1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_of_Ibelin_(jurist)_
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/JERUSALEM%20NOBILITY.htm#JeanIbelinJaffadied1266B<br/>
2 CONT JEAN Ibelin, son of PHILIPPE Ibelin of Rama & his second wife Alix de Montbéliard ([1210/15]-Nicosia 7 Dec 1266, bur Nicosia, Dominican Church).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "une fille Marie…et un fiz Johan" as children of "Pheli
2 CONC ppe…bailli de Chypre" & his wife, specifying that Jean was "conte de Japhe"[562].  "Johannes de Ybelino, dominus Berithi et Johannes dominus Cæsareæ" guaranteed the sale of property to the Knights Hospitallers by "Johannes de Ybel
2 CONC ino, filius defuncti Philippi de Ybelino" by charter dated Apr 1232 addressed to "Aelisia comitissa, uxore quondam Philippi de Ybelino, eiusque filia Maria"[563].  "Johan d'Ybelin le nevo dou sire de Barut" is named by William of 
2 CONC Tyre (Continuator) who says he was "le chevetaine de ceauz dou gait" in 1232[564].  In Palestine until Apr 1232, he fought at the battle of Agridi in Cyprus in 1232.  He was probably in Armenia for much of the time between 1234 an
2 CONC d 1247.  He was invested with the Barony of Jaffa before 1247, after the disappearance in captivity of Gauthier de Brienne Count of Jaffa, confirmed 1253 by Pope Innocent IV after which he styled himself Count of Jaffa and Ascalon
2 CONC .  Pope Innocent IV confirmed the grant of the county of Jaffa and Askalon to "Johanni de Ibelino, comiti Joppensi et domno Rametensi" for the foundation of a convent in Nicosia, by charter dated 26 Mar 1252[565].  He was appointe
2 CONC d bailli of Jerusalem 1254-1256.  He negotiated a treaty with Sultan Baibars in 1256, renewed in 1262 and 1266[566].  He was the author of the Assizes of Jerusalem[567].  The Chronicle of Amadi records the death 7 Dec, in 1266 fro
2 CONC m the context, of "messer Joan de Iblim"[568].  The Chronicle attributed to King Hethum II records that "the count of Jaffa, Sir Chuan" died in [14 Jan 1266/13 Jan 1267][569].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([1237]) KALAMARIA of Barba'ron, daughter of CONSTANTINE Lord of Barba'ron [Armenia-Hethum] & his second wife Alix of Lampron [Armenia-Hethum] (-Lampron [15 Jan 1263/14 Jan 1264], bur Sgebra).  Rüdt-Collenberg cites a colo
2 CONC phon of Yovhanes the bishop which names "Beatrice (mother), and Sempad, Hethum, Oshin, Basil, Leo, Vacaghk, Kalamarie, Stephanie and Hripsimeh, virgin (brothers and sisters), Philipp and Mariam Ibelin (children of Kalamarie)"[570]
2 CONC .  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Costans…connestable et…baill de la terre" and record that the daughters "dou baill" were married "…l'autre a Johan de Ybelin…conte de Japhe"[571].  Another manuscript of the Lignages clarifies that
2 CONC  she was "Marie, la fille Constans, le baill de Ermenie et seur dou roy Heiton"[572].  Smbat Sparapet's Chronicle records that "the countess of Jaffa Keramar, sister of King Hetum, who had come out of sadness for her father Kostan
2 CONC din…died in the fortress of Lambron" and was buried in "Skewra" in [15 Jan 1263/14 Jan 1264][573]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Ibelin & his wife had seven children:  
