1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/JERUSALEM.htm#JeanBriennedied1237
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         son ([1216]-[Jun/Jul] 1220).  William of Tyre (Continuator) records that "li rois Johans", on hearing news of the death of “Livon le roi d’Ermenie, pere de sa feme”, left for Acre from where he intended to go to Armenia
2 CONC  to claim the throne, but that he abandoned the journey because his wife died, and after 15 days later also “un fil que il en avoit de age de IV ans”[351].  He is named Jean in Europäische Stammtafeln[352].  That name probably rep
2 CONC resents a good guess considering his father’s name, but the primary source (if there is one) which confirms that it is correct has not been identified.  
