1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_IX_of_Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT David IX of Georgia (died 1360), from the Bagrationi dynasty, was king of Georgia from 1346 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Family
2 CONT
2 CONT David was the only known son of George V of Georgia. The identity of his mother is not known. The "Georgian Chronicle" of the 18th century reports George V marrying a daughter of "the Greek Emperor, Lord Michael Komnenos". However
2 CONC  the reigning dynasty of the Byzantine Empire in the 14th century were the Palaiologoi, not the Komnenoi. The marriage of a daughter of Michael IX Palaiologos and his wife Rita of Armenia to a Georgian ruler is not recorded in Byz
2 CONC antine sources. Neither is the existence of any illegitimate daughters of Michael IX. [1] The Komnenoi did rule however in the Empire of Trebizond. A Michael Komnenos was Emperor from 1344 to 1349. His wife was Acropolitissa. Thei
2 CONC r only child recorded in primary sources was John III of Trebizond. Whether John III had siblings is unknown. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Reign
2 CONT
2 CONT He ascended the throne succeeding on the death of his father George V the Brilliant in 1346. However, the kingdom’s stability and prosperity left by his father was not to last though, as the Black Death swept through the area in 1
2 CONC 348, decimating the population and producing severe economic crisis.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died, to be succeeded by his son, Bagrat V the Great in 1360.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Sindukhtar, daughter of Q’varq’vare II Jaq’eli, Prince of Samtskhe-Saatabago. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Bagrat V of Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT *Gulkhan-Eudokia of Georgia (d. 1395), who married first Andronicus Comnenus and after he died his paternal half-brother, Emperor Manuel III of Trebizond in 1379. Both were children of Alexios III of Trebizond, the first was an il
2 CONC legitimate and the second a legitimate son by Empress Theodora Kantakouzene.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/GEORGIA.htm#GiorgiVdied1346B
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         DAVIT (-1360, bur Gelati).  The Georgian Chronicle (18th century) records that "son fils David" succeeded after the death of King Giorgi in 1346[533].  He succeeded his father in 1346 as DAVIT IX King of Georgia.  The G
2 CONC eorgian Chronicle (18th century) records the death in 1360 of King Davit and his burial "à Gelath"[534].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' SINDUKHTAR, daughter of ---.  The Georgian Chronicle (18th century) records that King Davit married "la reine Sindoukhtar"[535].  Her family origin is indicated by the Chronicle of Michael Panaretos which records that "the
2 CONC  son of the emperor, the despot Lord Andronikos the Grand Komnenos" had been betrothed to [her daughter] "the king of Tbilisi´s daughter, the niece on the sister´s side of Achpougas"[536].  “Achpougas” has not been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Davit IX & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT --------
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT [https://www.allmonarchs.net/pmwiki/index.php/%D0%9F%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B8/%D0%94%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%B4IX%D0%A6%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%8C%D0%93%D1%80%D1%83%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B8 Давид IX, царь Грузии]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1346 году царем стал Давид IX, единственный сын Георгия Блистательного.
2 CONT
2 CONT В Грузии вроде бы всё шло хорошо, но XIV-й век был страшен для всех. В Европе начинался Малый Ледниковый Период, стремительно портился климат. Началась Столетняя Война и как раз в 1346 произошла знаменитая битва при Креси. В 1347 
2 CONC в Крыму началась Великая Чума, которая стремительно перекинулась на Италию, появилась в Константинополе и Трапезунде, а затем прошлась по всей Европе. В 1348 она пришла в Грузию. Погибло много людей и экономика существено пострада
2 CONC ла.
2 CONT
2 CONT В это же время Грузия пережила несколько набегов азербайджанских монголов (Чобаниды). В стране настал экономический кризис.
2 CONT
2 CONT Давид IX не смог совершить ничего великого. Он женился на Синдухтан Джакели и у него родились сын Баграт и 2 дочери: Гульхан-Евдокия, которую выдали замуж за императора Трапезунда Мануила III Комнена (1390—1412) и Гулшар, которая 
2 CONC была замужем за Иоанном Квенипневели, эриставом Ксанским.
2 CONT
2 CONT Давид умер в 1360 году в Гегути и был похоронен в Гелати. Царём стал его сын Баграт V.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://www.rgfond.ru/rod/33329?add_depth_up=2&open=/person/107187
