2 CONT 2.      '''   BALIAN Ibelin ''' (-Feb 1302, bur Nicosia, Franciscan Church).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "Balian, Bauduin, Johan, Heimeri, Phelippe" as the five sons of "Gui l'autre fis Johan de Ybelin, sire de Baruth
2 CONC …conestable de Chipre" & his wife[731].  The Chronicle of Amadi records that Henri II King of Cyprus had "doi barbani fratelli di sua madre…Balian de Iblim…siniscardo del reame de Cypro" who died in 1301[732].  Seneschal of Cyprus
2 CONC  1286.  The Chronicle of Amadi records the death in Feb, in 1301 from the context, of "Balian sinescaldo del reame de Cypro" and his burial "a li frati Menori"[733].  
