2 CONT
2 CONT a)         FAHREDDIN Kutlug [Qutlu] beg (-1389).  He succeeded in 1360 as Khan of Aqqoyunlu/Turkmen horde of the White Sheep.  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that on 14 Jul 1363 "the emperor´s son-in-law [error for bro
2 CONC ther-in-law] came down with his wife the Lady Maria the Grand Komnene, the despoinachat, to…Trebizond and was met by the emperor and entered the palace…camped near the church of John the Purifier for around eight days and then dep
2 CONC arted in peace honoured greatly"[1064].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1352) MARIA Megala Komnene, daughter of BASILEIOS Emperor at Trebizond & his second wife Eirene --- ([1328]-[1408]).  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "the emperor´s sister, the lady Maria the Grand Komnene
2 CONC  left" in Aug (dated to 1352 from the context) and married "Kutlu beg, Turali´s son, the emir of Amitiotai"[1065].  Despoina khatun.  The Chronicle of Michael Panaretos records that "the despoinachat Lady Maria, the sister of the 
2 CONC emperor…married to the Amitiote Kutlu Beg" came to Trebizond 22 Aug 1358[1066].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Fahreddin Kutlug had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT * From the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexios_III_of_Trebizond '''Wikipedia'''] page of his brother-in-law, Alexios III of Trebizond:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexios and his court strengthened their position by fostering peaceful relations with the Turkmen, cemented by marriage alliances such as that between the emperor's oldest sister Maria and Fahreddin Kutlubeg of Aq Qoyunlu in 1352
2 CONC .[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [7] Miller, Trebizond, p. 60
