1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Thierry Ganchou, Manuel had one son by his second wife Anna. Ganchou identifies him as the otherwise '''nameless Komnenos''' whom George Sphrantzes mentions in his history.<br/>
2 CONT This Komnenos had been the previous owner of the stallion Sphrantzes rode while campaigning in the Morea in 1429, and who married Eudokia the daughter of Manuel Palaiologos Kantakouzenos, but died before the couple could have chil
2 CONC dren.[16]
2 CONT
