1 NAME Pg Maharaja Lela Ong Sum Ping @ Huáng Sēnpíng
2 GIVN Pg Maharaja Lela Ong Sum Ping @ Huáng Sēnpíng
1 NAME Huáng Sēnpíng / Ung Sunting
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Huang Senping (traditional Chinese: 黃森屏), better known as Ong Sum Ping, (Ming Dynasty), who married Princess Ratna Dewi (Puteri Ratna Dewi), daughter of Sultan Muhammad Shah of Brunei, and was granted the nobility 
2 CONC title of Pengiran Maharaja Lela and elected Chief of Kinabatangan [1][1]
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reign of Brunei's third ruler, Sultan Sharif Ali, Huang Senping led the Chinese community and built a stone fortress (at present-day Kota Batu) [2]. He led an expedition to Sabah via the Sulu Sea. This expedition sailed
2 CONC  upriver to what is now known as Kinabatangan and made a settlement there but so far no archaeological evidence to identify the settlement. "Kina batangan" could mean "Chinese Strip". "Kina" (kee-na) is used by Kadazan Dusun which
2 CONC  similar to "Cina" (chee-na) used by Malay which refer the Chinese.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Chinese traveller, Wang Cho Lu, the tomb of Huang Senping was buried on a hill located about 2 km from the Brunei capital and there were Chinese inscriptions 黄总兵之墓 on the tombstone which meant 'Tomb of Commander H
2 CONC uang'.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In Brunei capital, Bandar Seri Begawan, there is a street named after him, Jalan Ong Sum Ping. The only street in Brunei with a Chinese name.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Brunei Museum has collection of his personal belongings which seldom display to the public.
