2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_of_Constantinople
2 CONT
2 CONT  Constantine XI Dragasēs Palaiologos (February 8, 1404 – May 29, 1453)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the last reigning Byzantine Emperor from 1449 to his death as member of the Palaiologos dynasty. After his death in battle during the fall of Constantinople, he became a legendary figure in Greek folklore as the "Marble Emp
2 CONC eror" who would awaken and recover the Empire and Constantinople from the Turks. His death marked the end of the millenium-old Byzantine Empire, the direct continuation of the ancient Roman Empire.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/XI._K%C3%B3nsztantinosz_biz%C3%A1nci_cs%C3%A1sz%C3%A1r
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/byzant/byzant8.html#K11
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Palaiologos family=
2 CONT
2 CONT The early generations of this family are confused and uncertain. The first certain ancestor is one Andronikos Dukas Komnenos Palaiologos, Gov of Thessalonica, +after 1246; m.his cousin Theodora Palaiologina; they had issue: 
2 CONT *A1. MICHAÉL VIII Dukas Komnenos Palaiologos, Emperor of Byzantium (1259-82), *1224/5, +1282; m.1253 Theodora Dukaina Batatzaina (*1240 +1303) 
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT **B2. ANDRONIKOS II Palaiologos, Emp of Byzantium (1282-1328), *25.3.1259, +Monte Athos 13.2.1332; 1m: 1273 Anna (+1281/2) dau.of King Stephen V of Hungary; 2m: 1285 Yolanda=Eirene of Montferrat (*1274 +1317) 
2 CONT ***C1. [1m.] MICHAÉL IX Palaiologos, co-emperor of Byzantium (1295-1320), *1277, +12.10.1320; m.1295 Rita of Armenia (*1278 +VII.1333) 
2 CONT ****D1. ANDRONIKOS III Palaiologos, Emp of Byzantium (1328-41), *1296, +15.7.1341; 1m: 1318 Adelaide=Eirene von Braunschweig (+1324); 2m: 1326 Joanna=Anna of Savoy (*1306 +1359/60) - Regent of Byzantium (1341-47) 
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT *****E2. IÓANNÉS V Palaiologos, Emp of Byzantium (1341-76)+(1379-91) -cr.19.11.1341, *18.6.1332, +Blachernai Palace, Constantinople 16.2.1391; m.Blachernai 28/29.5.1347 Helene Kantkouzene (*1333 +1396) 
2 CONT ****** ...
2 CONT ******F2. MANUEL II Palaiologos, Emp of Byzantium (16.2.1391-1425) -cr St.Sophia 11.2.1392, *17.6.1350, +after effects of a sroke as the mink Matthew 21.7.1425, bur Church of the Pantokrator, Constantinople; m.St.Sophia 10.2.1392 
2 CONC Jelena Dragas, Regent of Constantinople (*ca 1375/77, +as the nun Hypomone 23.3.1450), dau.of Konstantine Dragas, a Serbian noble 
2 CONT *******G1. IÓANNÉS VIII Palaiologos, co-Emp of Byzantium (1421-25), Emperor (1425-48), *16.12.1392, +31.10.1448; 1m: 1409 Anna of Moscow (*1393 +1417); 2m: 1421 (div 1426) Sophia of Montferrat (*1396 +1437); 3m: 1427 Maria Komnene
2 CONC  (+1439) dau.of Emp Alexios of Trapezunt 
2 CONT *******G2. Konstantinos Palaiologos, *1393/7, +1400/5 
2 CONT *******G3. Theodoros Palaiologos, Despot of Achaia, a scholar and mathematician, *1394/99, +1448; m.1421 Cleofa Malatesta (+1433), dau.of Malatesta di Malatesa of Pesaro and Fano by Elisabetta Varano 
2 CONT ******** ...
2 CONT *******G4. Andronikos Palaiologos, despot of Thessalonica, later became a monk, *1400, +1428; m.NN 
2 CONT ******** ...
2 CONT *******G5. '''KONSTANTINOS XI "Dragasés" Palaiologos, Emp of Byzantium (1448-53), *1405, +1453'''; 1m: 1428 Maddalena-Theodora Tocco (+1429), dau.of Leonardo II Lord of Zante; 2m: 27.7.1441 Aikatherina Gateliusaina (+1442) 
2 CONT *******G6. Michael Palaiologos, *1406/7, +1409/10 
2 CONT *******G7. Demetrios Palaiologos, Despot of Mistra, etc, *1407/08, +1470; 1m: 1436 Zoe Paraspondylina (+1440), dau.of Megas dux Paraspondylos; 2m: 1441 Theodora Asanina (+1470/71) 
2 CONT ******** ...
2 CONT *******G8. Thomas Palaiologos, Despot of Morea, titular Emperor of Byzantium, *1409/10, +1465; m.1430 Aikaterina Zachariaina, Bss of Arcadia (+1462), dau.of Centurion Asen Zaccaria Prince of Achaia 
2 CONT ******** ...
2 CONT *******G9. [illegitimate] Isabella=Zabia; m.1392 Hilarion Doria (*1372, +1423)
2 CONT ****** ...
2 CONT
