1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ref An Oriental Biographical Dictionary, Thomas William Beale. [Ya'qub Beg or Sultan Ya'qub. The son of Uzzan Hasan whom he succeeded in 1477 / AH 882, and became the king of the Turkman tribes called Aqqoinlu, or 
2 CONC the White Sheep. After his death, he was succeeded by his son Alwand Beg, who was defeated about the year 1500 / AH 996, by Shah Ismail I Safwi. (Safavi)].
2 CONT
2 CONT ======
2 CONT
2 CONT [ [Sultan Klialll (governor of Fars during his father's life time) succeeded to the throne, 
2 CONT and appointed his brother, Ya'qiib Mirza, governor of Diyar Bakr.] Sultan Klialll (governor of Fars during his father's life time) succeeded to the throne,  and appointed his brother, Ya'qiib Mirza, governor of Diyar Bakr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sultan Khalil proved weak, and the nobles of his court declared for Ya'qiib Mirza,  who, thereupon, advanced on Adharbayjan. In the ensuing battle near Marand I3 ,  on Rabi' II, 14, 883 "/July 15, 1478, Sultan Khalil lost his life
2 CONC  and Ya'qiib Mirza,  oocupied Tabriz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ya'qiib Mirzii ascended the throne. Ahmad Beg ibn Sultan Khalil and Kusa  Hajji Bayandar, rose in revolt at Shiror. and Isfahan respectively, but the rebellions  were easily suppressed. Similarly, in 886/1481-82, Bayandar Beg rose
2 CONC  in revolt at  Isfahan, but was &ilfed by the king's vanguard commanded by Sufi Khalil. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 887/1482-83, Ya'qiib Mirza invaded Georgia, and in the following year he  built a beautiful palace, named Hasht Bihisht (Eight Paradises), outside Tabriz 13 . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Being envious of Sultan Haydar's increasing power, Ya'qiib Mirza seized the  opportunity of helping Farrukh Yassar, the Shirvan Shah, against Sultan Haydar, who  had set out from Ardabil for the invasion of CharkaS,' and Daghistan
2 CONC . In the ensuing  battle, on Rajah 20, 893/July 1, 1488, Sultan Haydar lost his life, and his son and  successor, Sultan 'All Mirza aroused the suspicion of Ya'qiib Mirza, whereupon, in  the end of Rabi' II, 894/end of March 1489,
2 CONC  Sultan 'All Mirza, his brothers, Ibrahim  Mirza and Isma'il Mirza, and their mother, were imprisoned in the fort of Istakhr in  Fars.] ... [Ya'qub Mirza died at Sultan -Bud in Qara-Bagh on the evening of Safar ll 2 ,  806 3 /Dec.
2 CONC  24, 1490, and left three sons, namely: Baysunqur Mirza and Sultan Murad  by Gawhar Sultan Kh&num, daughter of Farrukh Yas&r, the Shirwan Shah, and Hasan  Beg by Qui! Jan Khgnum, daughter of Sulayman Beg]
2 CONT
