1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daine Nicole. Al enviudar, renunció al patronato de Sainte Marie de Grainville la Tenturière, que pretendían los monjes de Saint Wandrille, en virtud de Privilegio que les había sido otorgado por Ricardo, Duque de 
2 CONC Normandía, en 1204.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicole de GRAINVILLE was born circa 1280 in France. She was also known as Nicole de Granville La Tenturière. She was also known as Diane Nicola. She was also known as Diane Nicolle (perhaps someone in a later period misread the ti
2 CONC tle "Dame" i.e. "Lady" as "Diane). She was also known as Diane Nicole. Nicole de Grainville was Lady of Grainville-la-Teinturière, Cany-Barville, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France. The castle and fief of Grainville-la-Teinturière wer
2 CONC e included in her dowry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jean de Bethencourt (I) and Nicole de Grainville were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT  i. Regnault Bethencourt (III) was born circa 1310 at Caux, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT   ii. Jean de Bethencourt (II) was born circa 1310 at Sigy-en-Bray, Argueil, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France. He married Isabeau de St. Martin, daughter of Jean de St. Martin and Isabeau de Harcourt, in 1338 at France.
