3 CTRY Brunei
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dikatakan berasal dari Tanjungpura dan Sang Aji bermaksud '''Raja Suci''', gelaran Hindu bagi raja-raja Melayu. Penggunaan gelaran Sang Aji juga telah ditemui pada prasasti Gandasuli di Jawa Tengah yang menggunakan
2 CONC  bahasa Melayu dan Jawa kuno. Prasasti itu menyatakan bahawa mereka membuat arca Sang Aji yang diletakkan di sebelah utara prasada Sang Hyang Wintang. Gelaran Sang Aji pada prasasti itu ditujukan kepada Raja Sailendra bernama Dang
2 CONC  Karayan Sidabusu yang disemadikan di Sang Hyang Wintang Jawa. Mengikut sumber Sang Aji Kala telah mengadakan satu pertandingan kepada anakanda-anakanda dan anakanda-anakanda saudaranya iaitu perahu siapa yang terlebih dahulu data
2 CONC ng ke Brunei ia akan diangkat menjadi Raja Brunei. Dalam perlumbaan itu, Awang Alak Betatar telah berjaya memenanginya, dan seterusnya dilantik menjadi Raja Brunei menjadi Sultan Muhammad Shah.
2 CONT
2 CONT والله أعلمُ
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk%3AHistory_of_Brunei
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_Shah_of_Brunei The main source is from below: http://www.history-centre.gov.bn/kedai.htm or http://www.history-centre.gov.bn/eng-bookshop.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT For the above profile specifically, we can get this book (unfortunately in malay only):  http://www.history-centre.gov.bn/b-rampaisejarah-sinopsis.htm
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Old Brunei was a nation of Malay Hindu-Buddhists, according to a Chinese account of Puli, believed to be an early Chinese reference to Brute Old Brunei was said to have Similar Malay-Hindu Buddhist traditions and customs as Funan 
2 CONC or Kumlun, Chinese names for the first Malay state in Indochina during the early Christian era. Indians knew it as Sailendra, and Arab traders called it Kamrun.
2 CONT
2 CONT The early king of Brunei was called Sang Aji, or Reverend Monarch, a title of Sanskrit origin. The Brunei ruling dynasty changed during the early 1360s when Awang Alak Betatar, a prince from a powerful kingdom in western Borneo, a
2 CONC scended the Brunei throne. He became the first Brunei ruler and the present ruler is his descendant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Awang Alak Betatar was the first Brunei Raja to accept Islam, changing his title and name to Sultan Muhammad Shah (1363-1402) in honour of the Prophet.
