2 CONT
2 CONT [... Baysunqur Mlrzn ascended the throne. Differences arose amongst the nobles, 
2 CONT some of whom supported the king's uncle Masih Mirza. The result was a severe skirmish,  in which the pretender and most of his supporters were killed. Further, Rustam Mirza  ibn Maqsfid Beg ibn Amir Hasan Beg -eras imprisoned in t
2 CONC he fort of Alanjiq 8 ; but  another potential rival Mahamud Beg 6 ibn Ughurlfi Muhammad fled to Shah 'All  Parnak at Hamadan, where the Khutba was read in his name. Finally, Mahmud Beg  advanced on Adharbayjan, and encountered Bay
2 CONC sunqur Mirzii at Darguzm, but was  defeated in battle, and put to death after capture. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After this victory, Sufi Khalil, commander-in-chiei of Baysunqur Mirza, assumed  great power, which invoked the resentment of other nobles " . In the end of 896 8 /  about Oct., 1491, Sulayman Beg, governor of Diyar Bakr, advanced
2 CONC  on Adharbayjan,  and encountered Baysunqur D Mirza near Van 10 . The nobles, who were opposed to  Sufi Khalil, captured Sufi Khalil and Baysunqur Mirzii, and brought them to Sulayman  Beg, who put the former to death, and submitt
2 CONC ed to the latter, whereupon, they pro-  ceeded to Tabriz 11 . " ] ref: page 106 of https://archive.org/stream/HistoryOfShahIsmailSafawi-GhulamSarwar/119900259-History-of-Shah-Isma-il-Safawi-Ghulam-Sarwar_djvu.txt
