0 @N6000000002187705454@ NOTE Shamshi-Adad IV
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Shamshi-Adad IV was a King of Assyria from 1054 to 1050 BC. He was the son of Tiglath-Pileser I and usurped the throne from his nephew, Eriba-Adad II. The throne passed at his death to his son, Ashurnasirpal I.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Eriba-Adad II King of Assyria
1 CONT 1054–1050 BC Succeeded by:
1 CONT Ashurnasirpal I 
