0 @N6000000002187821736@ NOTE Smbat IV Xosrov Shum Bagratuni1,2
1 CONT b. circa 565, d. between 616 and 617, #6376
1 CONT Pedigree 
1 CONT      Smbat IV Xosrov Shum Bagratuni was was called 'Smbat the Multi Victorious' and was Presiding Prince of the Bagratids.. Sources: 1. Toumanoff, C. 'The Orontids of Armenia' in 'Studies in Christian Caucasian History' (1963) pp.
1 CONC 337-342. ; 2. Toumanoff, C. 'The Early Bagratids' in La Museon, (1949), pp.21-54. He was born circa 565. He was the son of Manuel Bagratuni.3 He was given by Kosrow Aparvez the marzpanate of the country of Hyrcania; made him princ
1 CONC e over all of those areas besides; who also exalted him yet more with honors and authority; loaded him with gold and silver; adorned him in gorgeous robes of honor; gave him the belt and sword which had belonged to his father Orma
1 CONC zd; assembled under his authority the Iranian and Armenian troops and ordered him to go to the country of his sway circa 610.4,5 He was given, by Kosrow Aparvez, the honor to be known as Xosrov Shum, adorned with gorgeous clothing
1 CONC , in a hat and muslin robes embellished with gold; exalted with unbelievable honors, a bejewelled camp, troops, and silver thrones, and gave him a small charge, the diwan of the land, four-toned trumpets and guards for his court s
1 CONC elected from the soldiers at court, circa 615.6 He died between 616 and 617.6 . His corpse was taken to the country of Armenia, to his native place of rest, and they placed it in a tomb in the village of Dariwnk' which is in the d
1 CONC istrict of Gogovit.6  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Child of Smbat IV Xosrov Shum Bagratuni: 
1 CONT   Prince of the Bagratids Varaz-Tiroc' II Jawitean Xosrov Bagratuni+   b. c 595, d. 645? 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S197] Toby Dills, "A Descendant of Antiquity," gedcom file from e-mail address (e-mail address) to Robert Stewart, 5 Feb 1999. Hereinafter cited as "Descendant of Antiquity". 
1 CONT [S1037] The House of Bagrat and DFA, online http://www.ut.ee/~votan/articles/bagrat.htm
1 CONT , Smbat Buratean. Hereinafter cited as DFA (Bagrat). 
1 CONT [S589] Robert Bedrosian (translator), editor, Sebeos' History (23 Washington Street, Long Branch, New Jersey 07740-5931: Sources of the Armenian Tradition, 1985), Chapter 10. Hereinafter cited as HoA: Sebeos' (7th C). 
1 CONT [S589] Robert Bedrosian (translator), HoA: Sebeos' (7th C), Chapter 17-19. 
1 CONT [S1167] Kirakos Ganjakets'i, Kirakos Ganjakets'i's History of the Armenians, Robert Bedrosian, translator (23 Washington Street, Long Branch, New Jersey 07740-5931, Sources of the Armenian Tradition, 1986), pg. 45. Hereinafter cit
1 CONC ed as HoA: Kirakos' (13th C). 
1 CONT [S589] Robert Bedrosian (translator), HoA: Sebeos' (7th C), Chapter 19. 
