0 @N6000000002187821718@ NOTE Prince of the Bagratids Varaz-Tiroc' II Jawitean Xosrov Bagratuni1
1 CONT b. circa 595, d. 645?, #6374
1 CONT Pedigree 
1 CONT      Prince of the Bagratids Varaz-Tiroc' II Jawitean Xosrov Bagratuni was was Presiding Prince of the Bagratids and Prince of Armenia after 628-631.. Sources: 1. Toumanoff, C. 'The Orontids of Armenia' in 'Studies in Christian Ca
1 CONC ucasian History' (1963) pp.337-342. ; 2. Toumanoff, C. 'The Early Bagratids' in La Museon, (1949), pp.21-54. He was styled Jawitean Xosrov [Forever Loyal to Xosrov] by the kings.2 Also called Varaztirots.3' He was born circa 595. 
1 CONC He was the son of Smbat IV Xosrov Shum Bagratuni.3 He was raised [by Xosrov] as though he were one of his own sons, elevated over all at court, and appointed to the office of cup-bearer, presenting wine to the king circa 613.3 He 
1 CONC was given the authority of the tanuterut'iwn by King Kawad, and made marzpan and sent back to Armenia with all of his father's belongings so that he would keep the land in a flourishing state, in 628.2 Presiding Prince of the Bagr
1 CONC atids between 628 and 631.4 Viceroy of Armenia in Byzantine Empire, Transcaucasia, between 643 and 645.5,6 He died in 645?.  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Child of Prince of the Bagratids Varaz-Tiroc' II Jawitean Xosrov Bagratuni: 
1 CONT   Prince of the Bagratids Smbat V Buratean Bagratuni+   b. c 625 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S197] Toby Dills, "A Descendant of Antiquity," gedcom file from e-mail address (e-mail address) to Robert Stewart, 5 Feb 1999. Hereinafter cited as "Descendant of Antiquity". 
1 CONT [S589] Robert Bedrosian (translator), editor, Sebeos' History (23 Washington Street, Long Branch, New Jersey 07740-5931: Sources of the Armenian Tradition, 1985), Chapter 28. Hereinafter cited as HoA: Sebeos' (7th C). 
1 CONT [S589] Robert Bedrosian (translator), HoA: Sebeos' (7th C), Chapter 17. 
1 CONT [S25] J. M. Hussey, editor, The Cambridge Medieval History, Volume IV The Byzantine Empire, Part 1 Byzantium and Its Neighbours (Bentley House, 200 Euston Road, London: The Syndics of the Cambridge University Press, 1966), pg. 780
1 CONC . Hereinafter cited as Cambridge Medieval History, Vol 4, Part 1. 
1 CONT [S25] J. M. Hussey, Cambridge Medieval History, Vol 4, Part 1, pg. 781. 
1 CONT [S261] Regnal Chronologies, online http://www.hostkingdom.net/regindex.html. Hereinafter cited as Regnal Chronologies. 
