0 @N6000000002322305303@ NOTE Prince of Taranto from 1406. Ladislas became a skilled political and
1 CONT military leader, taking advantage of power struggles on the Italian peninsula
1 CONT to greatly expand his kingdom and his power. He was under regency of his
1 CONT mother, Margaret of Durazzo, from age nine. He was expelled from Naples by
1 CONT rival claimant Louis II of Anjou in 1387. But, in 1399, Ladislas drove out
1 CONT Louis, who was no longer supported by France. Ongoing papal changes at that
1 CONT time served benefits to Ladislas, who was making expansions when he died.
